  "id": "transfer",
  "term": "transfer",
  "definition": "Transfer is the use of what has been learned in a new situation, showing that learning extends beyond simply finishing the original task. Near transfer refers to applying the same basic principle to new but similar problems, while far transfer refers to applying learning to more different situations, abilities, or points in time.",
